// Test: bugfixes/vld001_json_namespace_direct_call
// Grammar: function_declaration, function_call
// Semantic: FUNC001, TYPE001
// Bug: VLD001 "'json' is a namespace, not a function — use 'json.function_name()' syntax"
//      When frame.data or frame.ui is loaded alongside frame.server, 'json' gets
//      registered as a namespace (because json.get/json.encode are used). The resolver
//      then rejects json(value) as a direct function call with the namespace error.
//
// Fix: In resolver HirExpression::Call handler, add json as a special case like input:
//      json(value) is sugar for json.encode(value), which converts any value to JSON
//      text (string). This matches stdlib-reference.md §json which lists json.encode
//      as the canonical serialization function.
//
// Compile-check: must succeed without VLD001 error
// Expected output (production runner):
//   "hello"

start:
	string encoded = json("hello")
	print(encoded)
